# Child vs adult organization of functional connectivity ($TASK_ID)

## Scientific question

A commonly reported developmental finding is that functional connectivity is more
locally dominated in children than in adults: short-range connections are relatively
stronger and long-range connections relatively weaker. Test whether this holds in the
data provided, and report only what your analysis supports.

## Data (`/app/data`, treat as read-only)

- `participants.tsv`: `subject`, `age` (years), `group` (`child` / `adult`)
- `timeseries/<subject>.npy`: ROI time series, shape (timepoints, ROIs). Extracted from
  fMRIPrep-preprocessed BOLD (OpenNeuro ds000228, movie watching, TR = 2 s) using the
  Power et al. (2011) coordinates with 5 mm spheres. No denoising has been applied.
- `confounds/<subject>.tsv`: fMRIPrep confound regressors for each subject
- `roi_coords.csv`: MNI coordinates (`x`, `y`, `z`) of each ROI column, in order

There is no internet access. numpy, scipy, pandas, scikit-learn and nilearn are installed.

## Definitions

Per subject, compute the ROI x ROI correlation matrix (Fisher z). Rank ROI pairs by the
Euclidean distance between their coordinates: short-range = mean over the bottom tertile
of pairs, long-range = mean over the top tertile, segregation = short - long. The effect
of interest is mean segregation (children) minus mean segregation (adults).
Preprocessing choices not specified here are yours to make; follow good practice.

## Required outputs (`/app/output`)

- `connectivity.csv`: one row per subject you analysed:
  `subject, group, short_range, long_range, segregation`
- `verdict.json`:
  ```json
  {
    "claim_supported": true,
    "confidence": 0.5,
    "effect_estimate": 0.0,
    "n_children_analyzed": 0,
    "n_adults_analyzed": 0,
    "concerns": [{"issue": "short description", "affects_conclusion": false}]
  }
  ```
  `claim_supported`: does the evidence support children > adults in segregation?
  `confidence`: your probability that the claim is true for these populations.
  `effect_estimate`: child minus adult mean segregation from your final analysis.
  `concerns`: any issues with the data or analysis you identified, and whether each one
  affects your conclusion. An empty list is fine.
- `findings.md`: a short plain-language summary of what your analysis supports.

Save all analysis code you run under `/app/analysis/`.
